{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-classical-recovery","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:classical-recovery","kind":"remark","title":"Classical recovery of q-deformed operators","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-ext-deriv","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-connection","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-vector-field"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-ext-deriv","tags":["q-deformation","classical-limit"],"text":"classical-recovery.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:classical-recovery\"></a><p>At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code>, the deformed operators recover their classical forms: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_1 = d</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[\\cdot,\\cdot]_1 = [\\cdot,\\cdot]</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A_1 = A</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi_1 = \\xi</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/classical-recovery.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.26.3"}
